From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sven Eckelmann <sven@narfation.org>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 16:58:07 +0200
Subject: batman-adv: dat: fix printing of unknown 4addr subtype

If an unknown subtype of an unicast 4addr packets was detected in
batadv_dbg_arp(), it is printing the (known) packet_type instead of the
subtype. This must be switched to the subtype to have any kind of use for
the reader of the debug message.

Reported-by: Sashiko <sashiko-bot@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Sven Eckelmann <sven@narfation.org>
Origin: upstream, https://git.open-mesh.org/batman-adv.git/commit/?id=76a4fbd838f73ba7409dab6c41d4251bd1495b5a

--- a/net/batman-adv/distributed-arp-table.c
+++ b/net/batman-adv/distributed-arp-table.c
@@ -478,7 +478,7 @@ static void batadv_dbg_arp(struct batadv
 			break;
 		default:
 			batadv_dbg(BATADV_DBG_DAT, bat_priv, "* type: Unknown (%u)!\n",
-				   unicast_4addr_packet->u.packet_type);
+				   unicast_4addr_packet->subtype);
 		}
 		break;
 	case BATADV_BCAST:
